notes               = "Merged (July 2026) with `lovers-breath`, a duplicate of this poem created by the pages 61-69 bulk import, which did not dedupe against the file already in the repo. Ben's finished ===translation=== here is untouched. The Persian, machine pass, lantern and footnotes come from the import. That import had also staged an agent rendering in ===translation===, which per CLAUDE.md is Ben's slot alone; that rendering is now this file's ===lantern===, and the import's earlier, rougher lantern is superseded (kept in git history). The import's Persian is the better text: it keeps the trailing '...؟...' that leaves the grammar unfinished, and drops a stray tab character."
draft               = false

===persian===

های...
جنگ...
جانم را...
که در فاصله...
نفس‌های عاشقانه شکل می‌گیرد...؟...

۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Alas...
War...
My soul...
Which in the space...
Of a lover's breaths takes shape...?...

1368

===lantern===

Ah...
war...
my soul —
that takes its shape
in the space between a lover's breaths...?...

— 1368

===translation===

Ah struggle…

Y’know my soul was molded
In those distances
Between a lover’s breathing

===footnotes===

A fragment, and deliberately broken — the ellipses and the trailing "...؟..." leave the grammar unfinished. جانم را carries an object-marker (را) with no settled verb, so the line hangs: "my soul —" as something done to, or asked after. I kept the suspension rather than resolving it into a clean sentence. فاصله ("distance, gap, interval") is the same word that opens the page-61 poem; here the gap is between two breaths.
